cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "occ_sim: an open, physics-grounded benchmark of LED-matrix optical camera communication schemes"
version: "benchmark-r9"
date-released: "2026-11-06"   # Asia/Calcutta release-prep date; bump again if GitHub release is later
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Salvi"
    given-names: "Sanket"
    affiliation: "MIT World Peace University (MIT-WPU), Pune, India"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0898-2059"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SanketSalviNITK/occ-sim-benchmark"
keywords:
  - optical camera communication
  - visible light communication
  - LED matrix
  - benchmark
  - simulation
abstract: "Simulation-only, physics-grounded benchmark (EMVA 1288 sensor model, rolling shutter, Bayer CFA + demosaic, real corner finder) comparing LED-matrix OCC modulation schemes under equal optical power with common random numbers, bootstrap CIs and Holm-corrected claims. Includes shipped per-symbol error arrays, a sha256 manifest and a one-command reproduction script."
